# Hamro3D — Web Standards (Nuxt 3)

## Nepal-Specific Performance

Non-negotiable — most customers are on 4G mobile:

- Images via `<NuxtPicture>` or `<NuxtImg>` with `format="webp"` and `sizes` attribute
- All product images ≤ 180KB WebP for mobile data sensitivity
- Hero image preloaded via `useHead({ link: [{ rel: 'preload', as: 'image', href: '...' }] })`
- Below-fold images: `loading="lazy"` (automatic with Nuxt Image)
- No background video — too data-heavy for 4G
- Core gifting CTA accessible within 2 taps from homepage
- Target LCP < 2.5s on simulated 4G
- Leverage Nuxt's automatic code splitting per route
- Prefer CSS transitions (`transition-*` Tailwind classes) over JS animation libraries

## Rendering & Caching Strategy

```typescript
// nuxt.config.ts → routeRules
routeRules: {
  '/':                { isr: 3600 },     // Homepage ISR 1hr
  '/collections/**':  { isr: 3600 },     // Collection pages ISR 1hr
  '/piece/**':        { isr: 600 },      // Piece detail ISR 10min
  '/commission':      { ssr: true },      // Always fresh SSR
  '/our-story':       { prerender: true },// Static — rarely changes
  '/contact':         { prerender: true },// Static
  '/api/**':          { cors: true },     // API CORS
}
```

- Use ISR for content that changes occasionally (pieces, collections)
- Use `prerender: true` for static editorial pages
- Always SSR for authenticated/dynamic routes (commission flow)

## Responsive Architecture

### Desktop (≥1240px / `lg:`)
- Warm editorial, centered layouts, image-forward
- Hero at 100vh, product images min 500px
- Max-width 1240px container (`max-w-h3d-max mx-auto`)

### Tablet (768–1024px / `md:`)
- 2-column product cards
- Editorial text width preserved
- Hero reduced to 80vh
- 60px section padding (`py-[60px]`)

### Mobile (<768px / default)
- Intimate, personal feel
- Large text: H1 at 38px, body at 16px (handled by clamp tokens)
- Warm full-width imagery
- CTAs pinned bottom, 56px height (`h-14`)
- Max-width 390px content
- Touch targets minimum 44px (`min-h-11 min-w-11`)

## Accessibility

- Color contrast: cream `text-h3d-text` on plum `bg-h3d-base` — meets WCAG AA
- Semantic HTML: proper heading hierarchy, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`
- All images need descriptive `alt` text reflecting emotional intent
- Focus states: rose gold outline via `focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-h3d-accent`
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — use `motion-reduce:` variant to disable animations
- Support `prefers-color-scheme` awareness (brand is dark-first)
- Form inputs: visible `<label>` elements, not just placeholders
- Use `<NuxtLink>` for all internal navigation (provides prefetching)
- ARIA attributes on interactive custom components (modals, dropdowns, tabs)

## SEO & Meta

Every page must include via `useSeoMeta()`:

```typescript
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'Unique Page Title — Hamro3D',
  description: 'Brand-voice description of the page content',
  ogTitle: 'Same or adapted title',
  ogDescription: 'Social-optimized description',
  ogImage: '/og/page-specific.jpg',
  ogType: 'website',
  ogLocale: 'en_NP',
  twitterCard: 'summary_large_image',
})
```

Additional requirements:
- JSON-LD structured data for pieces: name, price (NPR), image, description via `useHead`
- `hreflang` tags for Nepali/English via i18n module
- Canonical URLs — handled automatically by Nuxt SEO if configured
- Sitemap via `@nuxtjs/sitemap` module

## Image Standards

```vue
<!-- Product image -->
<NuxtPicture
  :src="piece.image"
  :alt="piece.altText"
  format="webp"
  sizes="sm:100vw md:50vw lg:370px"
  loading="lazy"
  class="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
/>

<!-- Hero image (preloaded) -->
<NuxtImg
  :src="heroSrc"
  alt="Dusk atmosphere — handcrafted keepsakes in warm light"
  format="webp"
  sizes="100vw"
  preload
  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
/>
```

- Always use `<NuxtPicture>` or `<NuxtImg>` — never raw `<img>`
- Set `sizes` attribute for responsive image loading
- Hero images use `preload` prop
- Product images use `loading="lazy"` (default for non-preloaded)
- Provide emotional, descriptive `alt` text — not just "product image"

## Code Conventions

- Tailwind `h3d-` token classes for all design values — no hardcoded hex
- Component naming: `H3d` prefix, PascalCase
- Mobile-first CSS via Tailwind responsive prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`)
- HTML should read like a gift: semantic, clean, well-structured
- Devanagari text wrapped in `lang="ne"` attribute
- No inline styles — Tailwind utilities or CSS custom properties only
